            "image": "shopify://shop_images/265a3841deb5f332f889040ac22dbf129c9f33f8.jpg",
            "heading": "Burn, Baby, Burn",
            "description": "<p>When you burn, allow the candle wax to melt to the edges of the glass every time to prevent tunneling. This is especially important during your first burn!</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        },
        "care_item_tpgJR6": {
          "type": "care_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/4d578cc9158cc6e6c481b1b8e90eb2f6801f0764.jpg",
            "heading": "Safety First",
            "description": "<p>Never leave a lit candle unattended, and don’t burn your candle for more than 3-4 hours at a time. Protect the surface below your candle from heat by placing your candle on a coaster.</p>",
            "link_label": "Shop Candle Trays",
            "link": "#"
          }
        },
        "care_item_XQBmeb": {
          "type": "care_item",
          "disabled": true,
          "settings": {
            "image": "shopify://shop_images/0dcfb6541d0e5f806ac82ae7171fbf381a8e4c71.png",
            "heading": "Stop, Look, and Listen",
            "description": "<p>Do not burn your candle if there is less than ½ inch of wax remaining in the glass. Burning a candle without enough wax can overheat the jar.</p>",
            "link_label": "",
            "link": ""
          }
        }
      },
